Subject: [PATCH] Admin: Journey tags, the user journey's tagging for review
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A new admin module, Product → Journey tags (/admin/journey-tags), on
staging only (RELEASES.journeyTags). It classifies every moment of the
user journey map in eight tag groups: time of day, context, trigger, need,
state going in, time available, product surface and readiness. Each moment
has a review status (proposed, agreed, needs discussion) and a note.

Three views: Tagged moments (a table with stage, tag and status filters
and an editor per moment), Coverage (how many moments carry each tag, with
gaps flagged) and Taxonomy (edit, add or delete groups and tags; single-
or multi-choice per group; removing a tag removes it from every moment).
The first tagging of the ten moments is a product proposal. Moments are
read from the User journey's storage, so new ones appear untagged.
Export, import and restore; edits stay in this browser.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Je1v64McNyB6XEu6gFgM4C
